:"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I mostly want to see it perform the same as SceneTreeTimer, but the implementation of `is_stopped()` is a bit unexpectedly different. I wouldn't mind seeing it changed to `return processing` if it has mostly the same effect, since it would be easier to reason about.\r\n\r\nFor example, think about a case where I set a repeating timer to repeat every 0.1 seconds, but I am at less than 10 FPS. In this case, the timer will become negative and stay negative, and is_stopped() will be false, and get_time_left() will lie and say 0 even though the value is negative, yet a timeout event will be fired every frame. It's unclear what should happen but the current feels a bit wrong to me.\r\n\r\nAnyway I'm not saying we should fix everything about the timer class at once, just that we should try our best to make its behavior consistent.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107920#pullrequestreview-2955472219","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107920","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107920#pullrequestreview-2955472219"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107920"}},"submitted_at":"2025-06-24T22:05:32Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2962160528,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6wjvuQ","user":{"login":"jeronimo-schreyer","id":29764541,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzY0NTQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29764541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeronimo-schreyer","html_url":"https://github.com/jeronimo-schreyer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeronimo-schreyer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeronimo-schreyer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeronimo-schreyer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeronimo-schreyer/